<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §3 — the living bolt's own main think tree.

  WHY A WHOLE TREE AND NOT AN insertTag SUBTREE: RUT_LivingBolt is
  mechanoid-fleshed, so its inherited tree is vanilla "Mechanoid"
  (Defs/Core/ThinkTreeDefs/Mechanoid.xml, read whole this pass). That tree
  contains NO insertTag of any kind - the Animal_PreMain hook that
  mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors rides for the roaches simply does not exist
  on it. It is also built entirely around lord duties, overseers and
  JobGiver_AIFightEnemies, none of which a factionless, non-combat wild bolt
  has any use for. A dedicated tree is the honest route, and it is scoped to
  exactly one race: nothing else in the game names it.

  ORDER IS THE MECHANISM. Top to bottom:

    1-2. Despawned / Downed        - vanilla subtrees, same as every tree.
    3.   THE FREEZE                - RM_ThinkNode_ConditionalAttitudeBand
         sits ABOVE the queued-job node on purpose, so when it fires it
         pre-empts whatever figure the bolt was part-way through. This is
         the spec's "higher-priority conditional freezes the pawn (stand
         job, no wander)", structured the way vanilla structures every
         conditional freeze it has: a ThinkNode_Conditional subclass
         wrapping a plain JobGiver, not a priority branch buried inside the
         behaviour giver. The job itself is vanilla JobGiver_Idle
         (Verse/AI/JobGiver_Idle.cs - JobDefOf.Wait with an expiry), so no
         new job or driver is introduced for standing still.

    4.   ThinkNode_QueuedJob       - runs out the rest of a figure the dance
         giver queued. Below the freeze, above the dance, exactly so a
         part-danced figure yields to a freeze but not to a new figure.
    5.   THE DANCE                 - RM_JobGiver_ResonantDance.
    6.   Idle wander               - vanilla JobGiver_WanderAnywhere. This
         is the graceful-degradation floor: with the mod option off, or off
         a Rust Cathedral map, nodes 3 and 5 both return nothing and the
         bolt is an ordinary wandering mechanoid critter.
    7.   JobGiver_IdleError        - vanilla backstop, same as every tree.

  🔴 BAND DIRECTION - the one place this build departs from the kit spec's
  LITERAL words, and does so to keep its MEANING.

  The kit spec §3 says "a higher-priority conditional freezes the pawn at
  band 0". That sentence predates §1's build. §1 shipped (and documented in
  RUT_RustCathedralAttitude.xml and RM_BiomeAttitudeDef.cs) the opposite
  direction: band 0 is the CALMEST state - one warm drone layer - and band 4
  is the WORST, where the hum goes completely silent. Freezing the bolts at
  band 0 under those semantics would make them freeze when everything is
  fine, and dance hardest at the moment the hum dies.

  The frozen sheet's rule is not ambiguous: "when the hum drops, stop moving
  - the bolts freeze first." So the FREEZE follows the silence, not the
  number: freezeAtBandAtLeast is 4, the band where §1 kills every sustainer,
  and dance energy falls as the band climbs (full at 0, nothing at 4) so the
  dances visibly "go stiff, then stop" on the way up, exactly as §1's own
  player-experience paragraph describes. Both numbers are plain XML fields
  here - if the owner ever re-rules the band direction, this is a two-number
  edit and no C# change.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RUT_ThinkTree_LivingBolt</defName>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Subtree">
          <treeDef>Despawned</treeDef>
        </li>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Subtree">
          <treeDef>Downed</treeDef>
        </li>

        <!-- The freeze. See the band-direction note in the file header. -->
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.RustCathedralHum.RM_ThinkNode_ConditionalAttitudeBand">
          <freezeAtBandAtLeast>4</freezeAtBandAtLeast>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="JobGiver_Idle">
              <ticks>250</ticks>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_QueuedJob" />

        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.RustCathedralHum.RM_JobGiver_ResonantDance">
          <worstBand>4</worstBand>
        </li>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Tagger">
          <tagToGive>Idle</tagToGive>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="JobGiver_WanderAnywhere">
              <maxDanger>Deadly</maxDanger>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>

        <li Class="JobGiver_IdleError" />

      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
